    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n51578" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Κκ</span></b> , <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κάππα</span></b> , τό, indecl.,
		eleventh (later tenth) letter in Gr. alphabet: as numeral <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κ́</span>
		=
		<i><span class="en">
			20
		</span></i>, but <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">
			k'
		</span>
		=
		<i><span class="en">
			20
		</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
			000
		</span></i>. The numeral <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κά</span> (<i><span class="en">
			21
		</span></i>) is perh. used as one syll. in a metrical (?) Inscr., <i><span class="en">
			<u>IG</u>
			12(7).296
		</span></i> (<span class="entity">Minoa</span>), <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				like
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ζήσασα ἔτη έ</span>
			, at the end of a hexam. (?), <i><span class="en">
				<u>CIG</u>
				3025
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">Lydia</span>).</div>
